new file mode 100644
index 000000000..1a92aa6fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ZYAL/SUPER_REASONING_WORKFLOWS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,235 @@
+# ZYAL Super-Reasoning Workflows
+
+This document defines the target-agnostic workflow for using ZYAL to carry very
+large, multi-hour or multi-day projects through planning, implementation,
+parity, performance, hardening, and final signoff. Redis-in-Rust is a useful
+stress case, but this spec intentionally does not encode Redis phases.
+
+## Invariants
+
+1. The host owns the loop, stages, gates, budgets, sandbox, memory, and final
+   acceptance.
+2. Models produce structured artifacts, not authority. Model-only claims cannot
+   promote code or memory.
+3. Raw chain-of-thought is never stored. Durable memory is summary + evidence +
+   provenance only.
+4. Every phase has a signoff receipt before the next phase can advance.
+5. Parallel workers need declared disjoint write scopes and graph approval.
+6. Reference target repositories are read-only unless a human explicitly grants
+   a temporary destructive-operation lease.
+7. Required parity cases fail closed when absent, skipped, failed, or missing
+   required performance data.
+8. Performance closure must re-run correctness parity before promotion.
+9. Positive and negative memories both compound, but only after verifier or
+   reducer approval.
+10. A clean integration tree, rollback receipt, Jankurai gate, parity pass, and
+    phase signoffs are required for final done.
+
+## Canonical macro stages
+
+| # | Stage | Receipt |
+|---:|---|---|
+| 1 | `target_contract` | target/replacement request, success metrics, reference safety policy |
+| 2 | `evidence_atlas` | repo/docs/tests/benchmarks/reference evidence with hashes |
+| 3 | `behavior_inventory` | behavior map with APIs/protocols/storage/errors/edge cases |
+| 4 | `macro_plan_tournament` | blind planner candidates, critiques, reducer winner |
+| 5 | `phase_dag` | task DAG, dependencies, write scopes, proof lanes |
+| 6 | `scaffold` | skeleton/adapters/parity harness/CI graph plumbing |
+| 7 | `vertical_slices` | scoped implementation slices with parity-backed proof |
+| 8 | `integration_fusion` | merged lanes, conflict resolutions, graph refresh |
+| 9 | `parity_expansion` | generated and approved parity manifest |
+| 10 | `correctness_gap_closure` | missing/skipped/failed gap tasks closed |
+| 11 | `performance_gap_closure` | perf gaps closed without correctness regression |
+| 12 | `release_readiness` | final audit, rollback, docs, clean tree, acceptance packet |
+
+## Agent roles
+
+- `supervisor`: host-owned runner that schedules and gates work.
+- `framer`: turns the user request into success criteria and non-goals.
+- `atlas_worker`: retrieves repo/docs/tests/benchmark/reference evidence.
+- `planner`: proposes stage/task plans in blind lanes.
+- `critic`: falsifies plans, evidence, parity claims, and merge proposals.
+- `reducer`: combines only verified artifacts into host-owned decisions.
+- `builder`: implements bounded task slices in isolated worktrees.
+- `verifier`: runs proof lanes, parity, graph checks, and rollback checks.
+- `memory_curator`: writes verified/rejected capsules only.
+- `parity_generator`: generates target-switched cases and manifests.
+- `perf_auditor`: profiles candidate/reference deltas and creates perf tasks.
+
+## Graph database contract
+
+The graph database should persist at least these nodes:
+
+- files, modules, packages, functions, structs, enums, traits, impls, methods;
+- tests, benchmarks, docs, commands, protocol messages;
+- phases, tasks, parity cases, perf cases;
+- reasoning artifacts, memory capsules, model outcomes.
+
+Required edges:
+
+- contains, imports, calls, tests, implements, derives_from;
+- phase_owns, task_depends_on, reads, writes, changed_by;
+- parity_covers, benchmark_covers, verifies, supports, contradicts, reduces;
+- regressed_by and fixed_by for gap closure.
+
+Required queries:
+
+- `affected_tests(paths)` for checkpoint selection.
+- `parallel_safe(task_a, task_b)` for worker scheduling.
+- `blast_radius(diff)` for anti-sprawl pauses.
+- `parity_coverage(behavior_node)` for missing-case detection.
+- `gap_to_task(gap)` for correctness/perf closure.
+- `memory_recall(query)` for verified positive/negative memory.
+
+## Memory compounding
+
+Memory stores should split by purpose:
+
+- `target_contract_memory`: target facts and success criteria.
+- `phase_decision_memory`: signed decisions and reviewer objections.
+- `negative_memory`: failed plans, falsified assumptions, rejected designs.
+- `contradiction_log`: unresolved claim conflicts.
+- `parity_gap_memory`: missing/skipped/failed case history.
+- `perf_gap_memory`: perf regressions and successful mitigations.
+- `graph_memory`: durable function/test/parity relationships.
+
+Permanent write policy:
+
+```text
+status in {verified, rejected}
+AND evidence_level >= external_grounding
+AND source artifact id is non-empty
+AND raw reasoning is absent
+```
+
+Negative memory requires falsifying evidence. A rejected idea without an actual
+receipt is only scratch memory.
+
+## Parity and performance closure
+
+Each target adapter should declare whether it can run in memory/RamDisk mode.
+When available, parity should use that mode by default for speed and isolation.
+
+Required artifacts:
+
+```text
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/generated_manifest.json
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/approved-ci.txt
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/raw.jsonl
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/summary.json
+target/zyal/parity/<run_id>/gaps.json
+```
+
+The host converts each gap into a task with category, priority, graph scope,
+proof lane, rollback instructions, and reviewer requirements. The run cannot
+complete while `gaps.json` is non-empty.
+
+## Anti-sprawl rules
+
+- Initial edit scope must be declared before code changes.
+- Expanding scope requires graph evidence or human approval.
+- Diff budgets are checked per task, phase, and checkpoint.
+- Test deletion, assertion weakening, fake fallback data, and silent catches
+  block promotion.
+- Integration fusion may merge only branches whose proof lanes and graph
+  conflict checks passed.
+- Broad rewrites must be decomposed into phase-owned vertical slices.
+
+## Runtime acceptance checklist
+
+For a super-reasoning run to be considered complete, the host must verify:
+
+- target request captured;
+- evidence atlas written and hashed;
+- macro plan reduced from blind lanes;
+- all phases signed off;
+- graph export current after final checkpoint;
+- parity summary passed;
+- gaps file empty;
+- perf budgets checked;
+- Jankurai gate passed;
+- rollback proof recorded;
+- memory capsules verified/rejected;
+- final worktree clean;
+- no raw chain-of-thought stored.
+
+## Recommended proof lanes
+
+```bash
+rtk cargo test -p jankurai-runner port::tests port_runner::tests reasoning::tests
+rtk just zyal-port-fast
+rtk git diff --check
+rtk jankurai audit . --mode advisory --json .jankurai/repo-score.json --md .jankurai/repo-score.md
+```
+
+For live model proof, require explicit budget and fail closed on missing
+credentials, invalid JSON after retries, or exhausted call budget.
+
+## Example usage
+
+The generic runbook lives at:
+
+```text
+docs/ZYAL/examples/34-super-reasoning-port-swarm.zyal
+```
+
+It is intentionally parameterized by target/replacement and should be copied or
+templated for specific projects instead of baking target-specific phases into
+the ZYAL example itself.
